From 8c02f0e4c11b1a1e6c59b8c62f5dc5d391335508 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:23:07 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_kwallet: Form page with Wallets, Closing, Secret Service
 and Tray icon sections
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). KAuth save helper, kwalletd reconfigure, config keys and defaults are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- The master switch moved from a toolbar Switch action to the first row of the page, a checkbox "Use KDE Wallet"
  (was "Enable the KDE wallet subsystem", no "Enable" prefix) (kcm_kwallet/KWalletDEnabled). Everything below is
  disabled, not hidden, while it is off.
- Order by use: Wallets (default wallet + New…, "Use a different wallet for local passwords", wallet for local
  passwords + New…), Closing ("Close wallet: When unused for N min"), Secret Service ("Store passwords of other apps
  in KWallet" plus a one-line hint; was "Use KWallet for Secret Service Interface"), Tray icon ("Show icon in system
  tray", indented child "Hide it when the last wallet closes").
- Kirigami.Form/FormGroup/FormEntry replaced by Kirigami.FormLayout with separator sections (noun titles).
- Combo boxes have a fixed preferred width instead of filling the page; the hint label has a maximum width so the form
  keeps two columns.
- "Default Wallet:" -> "Default wallet:" (sentence case). Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_kwallet.tsv (outer repo).
- The local-wallet checkbox now acts on onToggled instead of onCheckedChanged: the old handler also ran when the
  page set the initial state and then overwrote LocalWallet with the first wallet of the list; with the async list
  below that would be undefined.

Speed: KCMWallet's constructor called KWallet::Wallet::walletList(), a blocking D-Bus call that can autostart
kwalletd (src/kcm/kcm.cpp, constructor). It now runs on a QThread; the combo boxes bind to walletListChanged() and
fill when the reply arrives (also used after "New…"). After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-013, HIG-017, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-023, HIG-047, HIG-058.
Not built yet. Unconfirmed: calling KWallet::Wallet::walletList() from a non-GUI thread (KWallet sources are not in
src/); no SettingStateBinding on the master switch because the kcfg entry name for kWalletDEnabled is not in src/.

